"""Typed raw-memory byte copy facade for `rt_bytes_from_raw`.

The file_bytes_typed leaf also declares the same provider with an erased
return, retaining packed backing across the bootstrap compiler's conversions.

Leaf module with zero imports. Callers that only need to copy a foreign
buffer into a `[u8]` import `bytes_from_raw` from here instead of
std.nogc_sync_mut.sffi.host, whose ~110 host externs (rt_tls13_*, rt_db_*,
rt_renderdoc_*, ...) would otherwise enter every closure that reaches them,
including the core-C bootstrap compiler, and stay undefined at link.

Facade function rather than an `export use ... as` rename: the seed
interpreter cannot resolve an aliased extern import
(doc/08_tracking/bug/seed_interpreter_aliased_extern_import_not_found_2026_10_19.md).
"""

@unsafe(reason: "raw runtime ABI for rt_bytes_from_raw", capabilities: [ffi])
extern fn rt_bytes_from_raw(ptr: i64, len: i64) -> [u8]

# Copy `len` bytes starting at `ptr`; the caller proves the range is readable.
@always_inline
pub fn bytes_from_raw(ptr: i64, len: i64) -> [u8]:
    unsafe(capabilities: [ffi]):
        rt_bytes_from_raw(ptr, len)

export bytes_from_raw
